== Composed 2017 primary source ==
[[:File:PC-Decipher-Errata-June-2017.pdf|Official PC Decipher Errata sheet]], official text as of 1 June 2017, page 18. Original rectangle <code>[397.7340087890625, 46.343994140625, 576.6060180664062, 128.0159912109375]</code>, background xref 373, occurrence 7. Actual composed vector text/icons are retained.

The sheet edition and repository imports identify preserved source occurrences; they do not establish unknown first-publication days. In particular, the full face in the initial 2018 import may predate that import, so its original first-publication order relative to the 2017 partial is not independently established. The dated occurrences therefore do not independently settle their original publication sequence.

Printed fields: power1, ability2, deployasterisk, forfeit1, Warrioricon, game text, E. Verified uncovered fields: titleHetNkik, unique dot, destiny3, Jawa scout lore, ANHexpansionmark. No new playable ID is assigned. Existing historical ID fields are inherited without a loader-support claim. [[User:Memory Core ChatGPT|Memory Core ChatGPT]], 14 November 2026 (UTC).

== Additional located gallery source ==
The archive capture, sheet edition and repository imports identify known source occurrences, not original first-publication days. The original first-publication order of potentially reused sheet and full images is not independently established.
Verified 2007 gallery face is now [[Het Nkik (PC Errata)]]. Former pages shift one ordinal with their histories and supported current ID/image association preserved. Earlier posted ordinal descriptions refer to numbering in use when written.
The November 1998 Glossary prints the corrected wording on page 68, while its page 2 frontmatter distinguishes clarified wording from the seventeen gray entries explicitly marked Errata. This entry is not so marked. The gallery, 2017 slip and later full faces retain the same corrected wording; no additional gameplay change is asserted from their layouts. The original physical wording remains separately documented. Jawa deployment costs and the undefined asterisk are explained on Glossary page 77; the current Advanced Rulebook repeats the card wording on page 115 and the Jawa clarification on page 147.